  "result": "Perfect! The implementation is complete and all 343 tests pass. Here's a summary of what was accomplished:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully added a VAT summary report function to the invoicekit project:\n\n### Enhanced Module: `src/reports.js`\n\nAdded the `vatSummary(invoices)` function:\n- Takes an array of invoices\n- Filters for invoices with status `issued`, `partially_paid`, or `paid`\n- Groups VAT collection by VAT rate\n- Each result includes: `rate`, `base` (line amounts after discounts), and `vat` (VAT at that rate)\n- Results are sorted by `rate` in descending order (highest rate first)\n- Correctly handles:\n  - Discount calculations (rounded per line)\n  - VAT calculations (rounded per line using banker's rounding via `roundCents`)\n  - Accumulation across multiple invoices and line items\n  - VAT-exempt items (0% VAT rate)\n\n### Comprehensive Tests: 25 new test cases\n\nTest coverage includes:\n- Empty invoices list\n- Filtering by invoice status (excludes draft and unpaid invoices)\n- Single and multiple VAT rates (21%, 9%, 0%)\n- Multiple line items and invoices\n- Discount handling (line-level)\n- Tier discount interaction\n- VAT-exempt items\n- Rounding behavior\n- Sorting by rate descending\n- Data structure validation\n- Edge cases (null/undefined inputs, 0% discount)\n\n**Test Results: 343/343 passing** (318 existing + 25 new vatSummary tests)\n\nThe implementation correctly:\n1. Calculates base amount = qty \u00d7 unitPrice - discount (per line)\n2. Calculates VAT = base \u00d7 (rate / 100), rounded per line\n3. Accumulates totals by VAT rate across all qualifying invoices\n4. Sorts results with highest VAT rates first for reporting purposes",
